From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett Lamy <blamy@Bretts-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 03:02:55 -0500
Subject: Make V8 the same on both sides in an Electron browser process

An Electron browser process has none of the annotations a renderer has. The
driver runs its recorded threads one at a time and keeps its heap at the same
addresses on both sides. So when its driver says so, V8 does the same thing on
both sides too, which a renderer's doesn't: the same bytecode, instrumentation
opcodes included, and the same flags.

Its GC is hidden from the recording, as a renderer's is, as commands from the
debugger allocate and would move it otherwise. So its schedule doesn't depend on
how long things took, and weak handles from the embedder are strong, so that
their callbacks don't run at points which can move.

Also what Node's bindings need, from the copy of V8 in Replay's Node, and hiding
the scripts Node and Electron run for themselves.

